{"ts": 0.137467, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m \u001b[90mStage 2 · Paths and the filesystem\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[93m◉\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m\u001b[90m○\u001b[0m  \u001b[93m2.3\u001b[0m \u001b[90m─\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 241}
{"ts": 0.13752, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.13959, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97m2.3 — paths: relative, absolute, dot, dot-dot\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nA \u001b[36mpath\u001b[0m tells the shell where something is.\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mRelative paths\u001b[0m start where you are now:\r\n  \u001b[90mnotes.txt\u001b[0m            a file in this folder\r\n  \u001b[90mpractice/notes.txt\u001b[0m   a file inside a subfolder\r\n  \u001b[90m../notes.txt\u001b[0m         a file in the parent folder\r\n  \u001b[90m./notes.txt\u001b[0m          same as 'notes.txt' (the . is this folder)\r\n\r\n\u001b[36mAbsolute paths\u001b[0m start from the root, with \u001b[95m/\u001b[0m:\r\n  \u001b[90m/etc/hosts\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[90m/usr/bin/vim\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[90m/home/alice/notes.txt\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[36m~\u001b[0m is short for your home folder. \u001b[90m~/notes\u001b[0m means\r\n\u001b[90m$HOME/notes\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[91mPredict before you act.\u001b[0m  If you're in \u001b[90m~/projects\u001b[0m\r\nand you type \u001b[92mcat notes.txt\u001b[0m, the shell looks for\r\n\u001b[90m~/projects/notes.txt\u001b[0m. If you mean a different folder, name it.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to take Stage 2's gate.\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 917}
{"ts": 0.140025, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 251}
